course: dictionary
lesson: 7072
title: Patriotic feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Patriotic is an describing word. It tells you how a person feels about their country: proud of it, and ready to help it. Read the words around it to find its meaning.
explain: «SlAva UkrayIni!» means «Glory to Ukraine!», a patriotic greeting. The words themselves are the clue: they praise a country, so patriotic means showing love and pride for your country.
explain: Patriotic feelings can unite people, especially in hard times. But too much can turn into hating others, so people learn the difference between patriotism and nationalism. Check any meaning by putting it into the sentence instead of the hard word.
fact: Patriotic is an adjective. It describes a person, a feeling or a thing.
fact: «Patriotic» means loving your country, feeling proud of it, and wanting to help it.
fact: «Patriotic» can also describe things that show love of a country, such as songs, flags and colours.
fact: Patriotism means loving your country; nationalism can go too far and turn into hating others.
fact: On national days such as Canada Day and Anzac Day, people sing patriotic songs and wave flags.
exercise: «Everyone sang patriotic songs and waved flags on the national day.» What does patriotic mean here? | Angry with your neighbours | Very tired after a long day | Sad and quiet | *Loving your country and proud of it
exercise: «SlAva UkrayIni!» means «Glory to Ukraine!», a patriotic greeting. What kind of greeting is it? | A rude word for a neighbour | *A greeting that shows love and pride for a country | A sad song about rain | A menu for lunch
exercise: Which of these shows patriotic feelings? | Hating people from other countries | Refusing to speak to anyone all day | *Singing your country's national song proudly on a national day | Throwing your flag in the bin
test: Patriotism means loving your country. What can too much patriotic feeling turn into? | Cooking a big dinner | *Hating other people | Being polite to visitors | Going to school early
test: On which national day do people sing patriotic songs and wave flags? | *The Fourth of July | Christmas Day | Halloween | Bonfire Night
exam: Mia says patriotic means angry with people from other lands. Which meaning is correct? | *Loving your country and proud of it, and wanting to help it | Quiet and shy | Very old and worn | Angry with people from other lands
